{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"The adjacent literature changes the ranking in an important way: recent controlled work finds that standard probes can mostly learn format, and verbalized awareness often has little behavioral effect. That strengthens the need for a crossed intervention design and weakens any direction that treats a classifier score alone as causal evidence. I’m cloning the official implementations that directly support prompt-pair construction, behavioral evaluation, and optional white-box probing."}}
